  "answer_tail": "n over the four files — not mental math):\n\n| File | Content |\n|---|---|\n| `t14_people.json` | ids 1, 2, 3, 4 |\n| `t14_scores.csv` | 1→30, 2→40, 3→10, 4→20 |\n| `t14_bonus.txt` | bonus recipients: **1, 4** |\n| `t14_rules.md` | rule: sum scores only of bonus recipients |\n\n**Join & sum:** Bonus recipients 1 and 4 → scores 30 + 20 = **50** (ids 2 and 4's non-bonus peers 2/3 excluded; shell output: `SUM 50.0`).\n\nEquivalent SQL (SQLite dialect, same result if you ever model this in a DB):\n\n```sql\nSELECT SUM(s.score)\nFROM scores s\nJOIN bonus_recipients b ON b.id = s.id;   -- → 50\n```\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 50",
